# TASK-012 — STAGED FOR AUDIT (cycle 1)

**Status in record: `pending`** — not advanced. Only the Auditor's sign-off permits
`completed`.

- build_id: `2026-07-20-sgt-bots-rori-academy-concierge-persona-runtime`
- Record revision: **15** (was 13 at briefing; +1 engineer envelope, +1 orchestrator
  verification envelope). `validate-build.ps1` → `ok: true` after each merge.
- Classification: **full crew** — four independent concerns, 9 files, one new interface
  (artifact-root override) and one new config file. Engineer implemented directly
  rather than spawning builders and disclosed it; accepted, same as the TASK-010 cycle.
- Wall clock: ~1h50m. Engineer run 1000s, QC reviewer 24s.

## Summary of the change

Nine files. All four ticket items delivered.

1. **Dead code.** (a) Removed the `ArtifactList` component and `ArtifactListProps`;
   **kept the file and the `ArtifactListItem` type export**, which has four live
   importers. The originating audit's wording ("remove dead `ArtifactList.tsx`") was
   inaccurate — this was caught pre-dispatch, adjudicated in the brief, and
   independently re-verified by the engineer. (b) Removed the unreachable
   `buildCreditBureauDisputeHelperReply` plus its 4 tests, plus 5 private helpers it
   orphaned.
2. **Stray artifacts.** Deleted all 13 inventoried targets (~3.3 GB): 5
   `*-20260531.tar`, `codex-oauth-fix-20260531.tar.gz`, `sgt-bots-rori-fix.tar.gz`,
   `sgt-bots-rori-fix.zip`, 4 `tmp-rori-*` files, `.deploy-src/`. `.deploy-images/`
   (4.7 G) preserved and gitignored. Six new `.gitignore` entries.
3. **Polling.** Network session-refresh poll `1000ms` → **`8000ms`**. The local 1000 ms
   countdown ticker was left untouched, so low-time nudges are unaffected.
4. **Flake fix.** `artifactRoot` made injectable on `createReportService`
   (`deps.artifactRoot` → `RUNTIME_ARTIFACTS_ROOT` env var → original cwd path). New
   `apps/api/vitest.config.ts` + `apps/api/tests/setup/runtime-artifacts.ts` give every
   test file its own temp directory. `report.service.spec.ts` switched off a
   now-defeated `process.chdir` pattern.

## Verification — orchestrator re-derived, not accepted as claimed

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| API suite ×3 from **dirty** `.runtime-artifacts` (23 files, never cleared) | **47 files / 386 tests, 0 failed** — all three runs |
| Expected test delta | 390 − 4 removed = 386 ✓ exact |
| Mini app suite | **9 files / 67 tests**, 0 failed (baseline match) |
| `@sgt-bots/api lint` | exit 0 |
| `@sgt-bots/telegram-miniapp lint` | exit 0 |
| Deletions | 13/13 confirmed absent |
| Protected paths | `.deploy-images`, `BLUEPRINT`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.buildwork/`, `Dockerfile.backend.hotfix` all present |
| `.buildwork/` not ignored | confirmed |
| Zero-reference greps | clean for all 7 removed symbols |
| CON-003 | historical docs still at 08:24 baseline mtime |

**Isolation proof (the strongest single piece of evidence).** `.runtime-artifacts` held
23 files with newest mtime 10:25:19 — predating the engineer's 12:55 start — and held
exactly 23 files with the identical newest mtime after all three suite runs. Test runs
previously wrote into that directory (that is why it was dirty). Zero writes across
three runs is only possible if the setup file ran. This also closes the QC reviewer's
"can't verify vitest.config.ts is picked up" item.

## QC review

**PASS.** Fresh blank-context reviewer, frozen diff. Per the standing instruction, the
diff excluded signed-off TASK-010/TASK-011 work: `DashboardShell.tsx` was reduced to
only the `1000`→`8000` hunk after I confirmed its other two hunks belong to TASK-011
cycle 2 (reconstructed by applying `task011-diff.patch` to the HEAD file and diffing).
No blocking or non-blocking findings. Its three UNVERIFIED items were filesystem facts
a diff cannot show; all three closed above.

